/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Functions: tags, asset, project, releaseId
 *   Constants: guard, importId, slotA, slotB, folderManifest, looseManifest, shared, releases
 * Tests
 *   - the file set is complete only when every manifest slot is ready, and its digest binds identities in manifest order
 *   - replaced and removed bound files are stale, while a slot confirmed after the run started is newly known
 *   - shared album and album-artist tags plan release searches, and only without usable tags the cleaned folder name, once
 *   - a shared barcode alone is a usable tag that suppresses the folder, and one file is looked up as a song
 *   - submitted text is planned with the shared credits, and a link, an over-long or an invisible-character name is refused
 *   - file names and folder segments other than a chosen root never reach a planned query
 *   - file evidence keeps manifest order, exact or legacy durations, draft Disc and Track Numbers, artist tags and identifiers
 *   - shared release IDs and catalogue numbers are usable tags of several files, while an ISRC counts only for one file
 *   - lookup accepts only a writable Draft v2 import project that no publication locks and that has not completed
 *   - candidates are distinct after normalization, capped at 25 in a stable order, and a release found by ID is fetched
 *   - admission prefers releases whose reported track count can match the files, and a search is complete only when every offered release that could match was admitted
 *   - details record missing, failed and compact fetched releases, and a release over the byte budget is omitted
 *   - ranking a record compares stored candidates with the current files and leaves incomplete ones unranked
 *   - candidates and ranking together stay within the record budget by omitting the largest fetched releases
 *   - ranking reads the iTunes localized names and the check of each iTunes-only candidate; an iTunes-only candidate is admitted once, within the shared bound
 *   - automatic retries run after 30 seconds, 2 minutes and 5 minutes, or a longer Retry-After of at most a minute, then stop; a first 503/429 within seconds
 *   - every fence write increments from absent, and only queued, running and retrying runs block
 *   - a new run replaces the previous results and carries only the automatic count, folder use and applied values
 *   - an automatic run intent is deterministic and UUID-shaped
 *   - the worker is idle without reaching the database while imports are disabled or it is stopping, and stops cleanly
 * @end-catalog */

/**
 * The metadata lookup record without a database: the bound file set and stale slots, the queries planned from shared tags,
 * identifiers, a folder name or submitted text, which projects accept lookup, ranking evidence, bounded candidates and details,
 * the retry schedule, the import fence, run replacement and the idle worker. All names, paths and identifiers are synthetic.
 */
